   {
    "id": "ca_mount_san_antonio_mt_baldy_devil_s_backbone",
    "name": "Devil's Backbone",
    "discipline": "mountaineering",
    "grade": "Mod. Snow",
    "description": "",
    "approach": "Park at the gate on San Antonio Falls Road off Mount Baldy Road and walk the road up to Baldy Notch, or ride the ski lift to the notch when it is running. Do not climb the slope under the lift, which is not permitted. From the notch follow the ridge road, then the trail, onto the Devil's Backbone, which runs east to west toward the summit.",
    "descent": "Return the way you came along the Devil's Backbone to Baldy Notch and the road or lift, as the ridge is the usual way down. When Harwood's snowfield blocks the ridge on the way up, the route skirts its lower southern edge to the saddle below Baldy's "
   },
   {
    "id": "ca_mount_san_antonio_mt_baldy_northeast_face",
    "name": "Northeast Face",
    "discipline": "mountaineering",
    "grade": "Mod. Snow",
    "description": "",
    "approach": "Start at Stockton Flat, where a gate crosses road 3N06 as it turns south toward Baldy Notch. Park near the gate and walk up the canyon to the west, taking the main fork that goes straight or right; the left fork leads to the northeast face of Harwood. Continue up the canyon until the broad gully and face come down directly above you, then climb it to the summit.",
    "descent": "The easiest way down is the Devil's Backbone, which returns to the gate at the start. From the summit follow the Backbone east, go down past the ski runs, and keep to the ridge that ends at the locked gate. Take care on that ridge: it splits several "
   },
   {
    "id": "ca_mount_san_antonio_mt_baldy_upper_south_ridge",
